Venetium 0026 - Windows ARM32 link fixes: x86-decorated TLS-callback /INCLUDE: names and the ARM64-only TSC guards.

BATCH-ARM-1 section 5, his decision (2026-10-03, "Yes, new patch 0026"). The re-run after 0025 compiled the whole chrome graph; 7 ARM32
links (chrome_elf.dll and six helper exes; chrome.dll and venetium.exe wait behind chrome_elf.dll) failed on the same undefined
symbols. 8 files:
- base/threading/thread_local_storage_win.cc, base/allocator/partition_allocator/src/partition_alloc/partition_tls_win.cc,
  third_party/perfetto/src/tracing/platform_windows.cc, third_party/boringssl/src/crypto/thread_win.cc: each picks its TLS-callback
  /INCLUDE: names (and the .CRT$XL? placement) by "#ifdef _WIN64 ... #else"; the else branch is x86's (decorated __tls_used,
  _p_thread_callback_base, ...), and ARM32 C symbols are undecorated (MSVC's ARM libcmt tlssup.obj defines _tls_used). Windows ARM32
  (_M_ARM) now takes the x64/ARM64 branch in both blocks: undecorated names, const callback data (lld folds .CRT into .rdata, as on
  x64). x86 keeps the decorated branch; x64/ARM64 are unchanged; MinGW does not define _M_ARM.
- base/process/process_metrics_win.cc, base/threading/platform_thread_metrics_win.cc, chrome/browser/metrics/power/
  process_metrics_recorder_util.cc, chrome/browser/metrics/power/process_monitor.cc: their Arm path (no constant-rate TSC) was
  ARCH_CPU_ARM64 only, so ARM32 called base::time_internal::HasConstantRateTSC()/TSCTicksPerSecond(), which Venetium 0017 removed
  for the whole ARM family in base/time/time_win.cc. They now use ARCH_CPU_ARM_FAMILY, as 0017 did. base/time/time.h (which still
  declares the two functions for ARM32, unused) is deliberately left alone: nearly all of Chromium includes it.
Reviewed before capture by two read-only lenses (ARM32 mechanism, other-configuration regression); the review found the two
chrome/browser callers that the first draft missed (chrome.dll links both objects directly).
Checked (RUNTIME, real arm-rt21 graph): the 8 ARM objects compile; ARM32 objects define R p_thread_callback_base etc. and carry
/INCLUDE:_tls_used; no ARM32 object references HasConstantRateTSC/TSCTicksPerSecond or __tls_used any more.

